     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:c66c0ca1-d216-410a-bd56-c26e320ea790",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ee73214c665b0206432c574576d17092?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ee73214c665b0206432c574576d17092?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ee73214c665b0206432c574576d17092?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ee73214c665b0206432c574576d17092?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAB-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Asger Askov Blekinge",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ac66c0ca1-d216-410a-bd56-c26e320ea790",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Actually, the enhanced content models now live on ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "http://ecm.sourceforge.net/"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "http://ecm.sourceforge.net",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The very restricted DS-COMPOSITE-MODEL datastream is an old Fedora problem. The fundamental problem is that DS-COM... was not made for content modelling. Rather, it was made for binding disseminators to datastreams in the CMA architecture.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Extending to optionals and cardinality,  while maintaining the disseminator binding have proved hard. The recent introduction of RELS-INT, ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "https://fedora-commons.org/jira/browse/FCREPO-441,"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "https://fedora-commons.org/jira/browse/FCREPO-441,",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "text": " could lead to an ontology-like description of datastreams, as rather ramblingly outlined in ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "marks": [
           {
            "attrs": {
             "href": "http://www.mail-archive.com/fedora-commons-developers@lists.sourceforge.net/msg00418.html"
            },
            "type": "link"
           }
          ],
          "text": "http://www.mail-archive.com/fedora-commons-developers@lists.sourceforge.net/msg00418.html",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
