  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Users want a way to describe richer content models than is currently possible with the Fedora 3.1 DS-COMPOSITE-MODEL.  One project that is beginning to address this is here:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/DEV/Fedora+Enhanced+Content+Models"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/DEV/Fedora+Enhanced+Content+Models",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However, Fedora's out-of-box DS-COMPOSITE-MODEL should also support cardinality and optional datastreams.  e.g. max and min, with some datastream # naming convention.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
