  "description": "<p>Users want a way to describe richer content models than is currently possible with the Fedora 3.1 DS-COMPOSITE-MODEL.  One project that is beginning to address this is here:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/DEV/Fedora+Enhanced+Content+Models\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/DEV/Fedora+Enhanced+Content+Models</a></p>\n\n<p>However, Fedora's out-of-box DS-COMPOSITE-MODEL should also support cardinality and optional datastreams.  e.g. max and min, with some datastream # naming convention.</p>",
